    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesis</span></b> , is, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Umbria on the
				river Æsis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">COL. AESIS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3899</span></i>
			.—Whence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesinas</span></b> ,
			ātis, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Æsis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 241</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesinātes</span></b> ,
			ium, m., <i>the inhabitants
				of Æsis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14, 19, §
		113</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
